                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I’m going to be honest, this game is by no means perfect and does have issues, but I really enjoyed playing this game. This is the first time I played it on a desktop (the first time I originally played it was on my iPad in 2014). It’s a shame to see that a lot of the reviews dislike this game, and I get it for certain reasons. \n\nIf you enjoy 2D platformers, then this game is honestly engaging and a difficult challenge. A lot of it is high-paced shooting.\n\nThe good\n\n- The gameplay is honestly fairly decent, but not that complicated. You have 3 planes that you can pick from: the Beast, the Freshmen, and Tyker’s. All 3 play differently, but the beast is the best one that there is since he does the most damage, and has the most health.\n\n- The bosses are very funny to play against, and are also very difficult and give you a actually good challenge to fight against, especially the fire plane. I will say the final boss is incredibly difficult to beat. As well as the Zeppelin. \nAlthough some of the levels are repetitive, there is enough to keep you engaged and to keep on playing.\n\n- I honestly like the art style. I think it fits very well.  \n\nThe bad \n\n- The grind in this game is annoying, but it’s not as bad as others have made it out to be. For the most part, you will just be playing the first boss over and over again until you can afford the upgrades in the game. Which the first boss is very quick to beat, so it’s fairly quick.\n\n- The same 2 music tracks are used in the entire game; there's no variety at all.\n\n- The Freshmen is basically useless. You will mostly play the beast for the whole game. Tyker’s is really only useful on the final boss.",
